  "type": "MCQ",
  "question": "Let $K$ be the set of all points $(x,y)$ such that $|x|+|y|\\le1$. Given a point $A$ in the plane, let $F_A$ be the point in $K$ which is closest to $A$. Then the points $A$ for which $F_A=(1,0)$ are",
  "options": {
    "A": "all points $A=(x,y)$ with $x>1$;",
    "B": "all points $A=(x,y)$ with $x\\ge y+1$ and $x\\ge1-y$;",
    "C": "all points $A=(x,y)$ with $x\\ge1$ and $y=0$;",
    "D": "all points $A=(x,y)$ with $x\\ge0$ and $y=0$."
  },
  "answer": "B",
